cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its teaching materials, please cite it as below."
title: "手写数字实验台 / Handwritten Digit Lab"
abstract: "A browser-based teaching demo in two lessons. Lesson 1: draw a digit and watch three networks trained on MNIST (fully connected only, a small CNN and a standard CNN) recognise it, with a live architecture diagram, per-layer activations, an occlusion heat map and neuron knockout. Lesson 2: the same convolutional encoder, trained as an autoencoder, squeezes every digit into 2 numbers - a point on a map - and the decoder draws a digit-like 'shadow' from any point; it also compares bottleneck sizes and shows how much of the input survives in each layer of the recognition network. All networks run in pure JavaScript. Part of the AI 教学演示案例 / AI Teaching Demos series."
type: software
